<title>USA: Heilig-Meyers buying assets of 20 stores.</title>
<headline>Heilig-Meyers buying assets of 20 stores.</headline>
<dateline>RICHMOND, Va. 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Heilig-Meyers Co Tuesday said it has signed a letter of intent to buy certain assets relating to 20 stores of McMahan's Furniture Company.</p>
<p>Accounts receivable, inventories and miscellaneous assets will be purchased by Heilig-Meyers. Closing for the purchase is scheduled for the middle of September, it said.</p>
<p>The transaction does not include 22 McMahan's Furniture Stores in California and Oregon that are owned and operated by relatives of James A. McMahan.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
